id: decisions/044-verdict-arity
title: "Verdicts about people keep unknown"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'verdict-arity'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: verdict-arity
axis_gloss: "whether a gate, consent or classification resolves to yes/no, or carries intermediate and qualified values"
poles:
  a: graded-verdict
  b: binary-verdict
split: lone-exception
draft_status: full
leverage: 5.3
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(11) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  Must every gate, consent and status be able to say unknown or partly, or are
  there records where plain yes or no is the honest shape?

why_it_matters: >
  Four written rules keep failure, dispute, discrepancy and residual lacuna
  representable and refuse to collapse consent or ratification into a boolean;
  the two binary shapes in the tree are an observation's lifecycle (accepted or
  superseded) and a ceiling of three ranked paths, both test-pinned. A bot
  inherits whether it may round one missing signature to true; a child Yawn
  inherits whether silence is recorded as unknown or as no.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    9 judgments sit at graded-verdict (4 authored) and 2 at binary-verdict (0
    authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether unknown is a default the system writes when nobody spoke, or only a
    value a person asserts; the three consent examples disagree by silence.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      Every verdict field carries at least a third value for unknown, withheld or
      disputed. A boolean is never used for consent, ratification, a gate result, or
      an epistemic status.
    cost: "observation.v1's status enum gains a third value it cannot honestly use; the receipt tests that pin two-value fields are loosened."
    risk: "An append-only record acquires a state (draft, rejected, archived) that implies a mutation it cannot undergo, which is the reason J1108 gives for two values."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "A schema lint over schemas/*.json rejecting any boolean property whose name contains consent, ratified, cleared, or approved."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0400"
      - "J0402"
      - "J0517"
      - "J0530"
      - "J0531"
      - "J0578"
  - name: B
    description: >
      Verdicts are binary. Unknown is resolved before recording; a gate is clear or
      not; consent is yes or no.
    cost: "Collapsing recorded_with_consent: unknown, partially_ratified, and the nine answer statuses; deleting the turn-close invariants."
    risk: "Silence reads as no or as yes; withholding reads as skipping; a partial ratification rounds to a lie in one direction."
    reversibility: false
    proof_needed: "None on this side beyond the two lifecycle enums already pinned."
    evidence_for:
      - "J1108"
      - "J1217"
  - name: C
    description: >
      Anything that describes a person or a claim (consent, ratification, gate
      result, answer status, epistemic status) carries at least unknown and, where
      it applies, partial or disputed. Binary is allowed only for the lifecycle of
      an append-only record (accepted or superseded) and for bounded counts, where a
      third value would imply a mutation or a choice the record cannot make.
    cost: "One sentence in core/proof-and-boundary.yawn; the three recorded_with_consent values across examples/ unified into one enum in schemas/."
    risk: "The line between describes-a-person and lifecycle needs one judgment per new field."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "Keep tests/observation-state-v1.test.mjs pinning accepted or superseded; extend tests/state-substrate-v1.test.mjs ('multi-principal desires preserve privacy and cannot self-ratify a shared target') to assert ratification is two lists plus a three-state status; add a schema lint that no boolean is named consent, ratified, cleared or approved."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0400"
      - "J0402"
      - "J0517"
      - "J0530"
      - "J0531"
      - "J0578"
      - "J1108"
      - "J1217"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.8
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    All four authored judgments are graded and give reasons: collapsing lets
    silence read as unknown and withholding as skipping. The two binary judgments
    are both proof-attached and neither is a verdict about a person or a claim:
    J1108 is an append-only lifecycle where a third value would be a lie about
    mutability, and J1217 is a count ceiling. C writes down the distinction the
    tests already draw. The only cost is a sentence and an enum.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "core/proof-and-boundary.yawn states which fields must carry unknown or partial and which may be binary"
    - "A lint in tests/ rejects boolean consent, ratified, cleared or approved properties in schemas/ and passes"
    - "recorded_with_consent is one enum with yes, no, unknown declared in schemas/ and every example uses it"

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A new schema lands with ratified: boolean or a gate result whose only values
    are true and false.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0400"
  - "J0402"
  - "J0517"
  - "J0530"
  - "J0531"
  - "J0578"
  - "J1108"
  - "J1217"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
